                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is totally unique, the store page says based off of British comics. There are 4 characters and the landscape is designed around their abilities. You start with one character at a time, and you can only reach certain areas at a later point when you have the others. Then they team up in 2 pairs, and you switch back and forth between them at totems/save points, and it doesn’t take much catching up to get them to the same place, but you are doing the same thing twice. Then all 4 met together, and I stopped playing. Before there was one glowing spot on the map you had to trek to, or a linear plot. Then there were 2 different spots in opposite directions and no clue as to which character goes which way. I tried one way and it wasn’t working and I tried the other way, I kept getting stuck. No way am I going to separately maneuver 4 characters to the same place with a set of limitations each, and not even knowing if I’m going the right way. The puzzle aspect of traversal is clearly well thought out, I might have just hit a hard part. I didn’t have the mental endurance or patience to make it through, but if you enjoy getting lost in a deeply complex map system, there is a lot of content here.",
